# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Absolute paths into user-writable, temporary or package-manager folders that may remain inside an engine's
# Mach-O and PE files, and why each is harmless. tools/engine-guard.py refuses any hit not matched here; there is
# no option to skip that check. An allowance names one engine exactly, so a new engine is reviewed again.
# Format (tab separated): engine  file glob (relative to the engine's top folder)  regular expression  reason
# Keep this list short: every line needs a reason someone can check in the source.
engine-arm64-11.18-2	lib/wine/aarch64-unix/ntdll.so	^/tmp/\.wine-%u/server-%llx-%llx$	Wine's wineserver socket folder (dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c). Created by Wine with mode 0700; client and server stop unless it is a directory owned by the user with no group or other access (server/request.c create_dir). Runtime IPC, not a file Wine loads code or data from.
engine-arm64-11.18-2	bin/wineserver	^/tmp/\.wine-%u$	The same socket folder, server side (server/request.c), with the same ownership and mode checks.
engine-arm64-11.18-2	bin/wineserver	^/usr/local/share/wine/nls$	Last-resort read-only fallback for l_intl.nls (server/unicode.c load_intl_file), tried only if the engine's own share/wine/nls/l_intl.nls (shipped) cannot be opened. A case-mapping data table, opened O_RDONLY; no code. The Intel engine removes it (its patch 0002); the next arm64 engine should too.
engine-arm64-11.18-2	lib/wine/aarch64-unix/crypt32.so	^/usr/local/share/certs/$	Read-only fallback root-certificate folder (dlls/crypt32/unixlib.c), used only if the macOS keychain (read first) returns no root certificate at all. The Intel engine removes it (its patch 0003); the next arm64 engine should too.
engine-arm64-11.18-2	lib/wine/*-windows/dbghelp.dll	^/usr/local/lib:/lib:/usr/lib$	dbghelp's default search path for unix debug symbols (dlls/dbghelp/macho_module.c), used only when a debugger asks for symbols of a host library; reads them, never runs them.
engine-arm64-11.18-2	lib/wine/*-windows/winemenubuilder.exe	^/usr/local/share/:/usr/share/$	XDG_DATA_DIRS default of winemenubuilder (Linux desktop menus); the engine turns winemenubuilder off (WINEDLLOVERRIDES winemenubuilder.exe=d) and it only reads there.
engine-arm64-11.18-2	lib/wine/*-windows/wineps.drv	^/tmpmtrx matrix def$	Not a path: PostScript source text in the printer driver ("/tmpmtrx" is a PostScript name).
engine-arm64-11.18-2	lib/wine/aarch64-windows/*fex.dll	^/tmp/perf-\{\}\.map$	FEX's JIT symbol map (FEXCore/Source/Common/JitSymbols.cpp), written only when a FEX JIT-naming debug option is on (off by default); inside a Windows DLL the path resolves inside the Wine prefix (C:\tmp\...), not on the Mac.
engine-arm64-11.18-2	lib/wine/aarch64-windows/xtajit*.dll	^/tmp/perf-\{\}\.map$	The same FEX DLLs under the names Wine loads them by.
engine-arm64-11.18-2	lib/wine/aarch64-windows/*fex.dll	^/Users/runner/work/llvm-mingw/llvm-mingw/llvm-project/(libcxxabi|libunwind)/src/	__FILE__ strings inside libc++abi and libunwind, which llvm-mingw's release built on GitHub's CI (user "runner") and FEX links statically: text of assertion and abort messages, never opened. Not a path on any Mac; rebuilding llvm-mingw's runtime is the only way to change it.
engine-arm64-11.18-2	lib/wine/aarch64-windows/xtajit*.dll	^/Users/runner/work/llvm-mingw/llvm-mingw/llvm-project/(libcxxabi|libunwind)/src/	The same, in the copies Wine loads.
engine-x86_64-11.18-1	lib/wine/x86_64-unix/ntdll.so	^/tmp/\.wine-%u/server-%llx-%llx$	Wine's wineserver socket folder (dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c). Created by Wine with mode 0700; client and server stop unless it is a directory owned by the user with no group or other access (server/request.c create_dir). Runtime IPC, not a file Wine loads code or data from.
engine-x86_64-11.18-1	bin/wineserver	^/tmp/\.wine-%u$	The same socket folder, server side (server/request.c), with the same ownership and mode checks.
engine-x86_64-11.18-1	lib/wine/*-windows/dbghelp.dll	^/usr/local/lib:/lib:/usr/lib$	dbghelp's default DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH (dlls/dbghelp/macho_module.c), searched only when a debugger asks for the symbols of a host library it cannot find by its own path. On an Intel Mac /usr/local may be Homebrew's and user-writable, but dbghelp only reads symbol tables there as data; it never loads or runs them, and anyone who can write there already runs code as that user.
engine-x86_64-11.18-1	lib/wine/*-windows/winemenubuilder.exe	^/usr/local/share/:/usr/share/$	XDG_DATA_DIRS default of winemenubuilder (programs/winemenubuilder/winemenubuilder.c, Linux desktop menus); the engine turns winemenubuilder off (WINEDLLOVERRIDES winemenubuilder.exe=d) and it only reads there.
engine-x86_64-11.18-1	lib/wine/*-windows/wineps.drv	^/tmpmtrx matrix def$	Not a path: PostScript source text in the printer driver (dlls/wineps.drv/ps.c; /tmpmtrx is a PostScript name).
